/-!
# SU(3) Loop Group ↔ Braid Group B₃ Duality

This file formalizes a finite algebraic shadow of a proposed SU(3)
loop/braid picture: adjacent color permutations, q-scaled braid actions, and
diagonal Cantor-loop gauge covariance.  It does not formalize loop groups,
DHR superselection sectors, or equivalences with quantum groups.

The Cuntz algebra O₄ on the Cantor boundary is the algebraic realization
of the quantum group SU_q(3) at a root of unity (the thermal Unruh
parameter q_β).  The braid generators σ₁, σ₂ act as swap12, swap23 on
the three parafermion color lanes — this is the B₃ → S₃ projection
followed by the Weyl group action on the Gell-Mann generators.

The loop/braid duality:
  SU(3) [bulk, continuous Lie algebra]
    → L(SU(3)) [boundary, loop group]
    → SU_q(3) [quantum group, q = qRapidity(β)]
    → O₄ [Cuntz algebra, Cantor boundary]
    → B₃ [braid group, parafermion color-lane permutations]

Zero sorries.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace SU3LoopBraidDuality

